<title>USA: Ill. Gov sets sites for new correctional centers.</title>
<headline>Ill. Gov sets sites for new correctional centers.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois Gov. Jim Edgar has announced plans to build a new $69 million adult prison in southeastern Illinois and a $45 million juvenile facility in western Illinois.</p>
<p>Both the 1,800-bed medium-security adult facility set for Lawrence County and the 400-bed medium-security juvenile center planned for Kewanee are to be completed in 1999, Edgar said in a statement.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
